  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer of resistance <math><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> has <math><mn>50</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math> divisions on its scale and has sensitivity of <math><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> . It is to be converted to voltmeter with three ranges, of <math><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The appropriate circuit to do so is:",
